WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.100
Your Majesty,

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.150
King Edward V.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.150
Have no fear.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.860
I've come to save you.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.530
Who are you?!

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.490
You have nothing to fear from me.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.250
Look: I've brought you sweet treats.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.460
Did my mother send you?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.080
The <i>true king</i> has many allies.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:32.670
As we speak, the palace is abuzz with
talk that Richard's son is illegitimate.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.890
Support for him has been on
the wane since his accession.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:44.730
Everyone is saying that, after all,
Edward V was the rightful king.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.480
It took those fools long
enough to realize.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.940
The palace eagerly awaits
Your Majesty's return.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.280
Now go, before the guards notice.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.910
Make haste. Your supporters
await you at the gate.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.960
Await the true king's return.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:12.840
When time is out of joint, the hero
saves the true king and sets it right.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.420
Not for himself--oh, no--

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.430
but for justice only.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.510
But what is "justice"?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.850
The right bloodline? The proper ritual?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.390
Not at all.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:27.270
It's who everyone likes.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.230
Dreadful news!

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.740
The children have escaped the Tower!

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.200
Fate has been decided from the first.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.660
York of the white rose.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.330
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:55.710
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.340
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.980
What's all the fuss?

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.400
The children in the Tower escaped!

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.530
What?!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.370
Fortunately, they were returned
to the Tower at once,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.240
but the intruder hasn't been found.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.370
Unhand me! I am King Edward V!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.580
Richard!

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.590
I hear your son's bloodline is in doubt!

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:00.210
And no wonder: you <i>are</i> a demon!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.130
Take them away!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.430
Just you watch!

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.550
Everyone will beg me to take
my throne back soon!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.970
I have hordes of supporters!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.980
I knew those rumors were to blame.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.730
If this is all according
to our enemy's script,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.990
then that boy is a liability.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.360
Henry, shall I save you?

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.830
If you'll give me what I desire...

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.450
What do you mean?

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:37.670
You aren't my king,
but my king does love you.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.460
If you teach me about love,
I will grant your wish.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.680
I'll kill whomever you desire.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.480
Don't make a fuss.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.360
I don't want it said that I took ill
so soon after my accession.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.860
But the queen ordered me
to summon physicians at once.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.660
I assume you refused.
How could I show a physician this body?

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:11.370
Your coronation in York
is fast approaching.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:16.580
She refuses to make the journey
if your health is poor.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.250
I can't approve a long
journey while ill either.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.050
Then bring <i>her</i> to me.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.930
Buckingham did say he had
engaged her as a royal physician.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.020
You are still a criminal.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.400
If you harm His Majesty,
you may not live to regret it.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.240
It's an honor to see you again,

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.450
Your Royal Majesty.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.120
By your leave.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.500
Any pain? Any changes in your diet?

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.540
No.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.420
Nausea, perhaps?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.550
Well... I've had much on my mind.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.420
Have you been feverish?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.510
How dare you?!

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.140
I can't diagnose him without touching him.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.390
I've never examined his body before.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.860
Would you please show me everything?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.990
Show no surprise.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.110
I forbid it.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.080
May I draw the curtains?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.250
That's all for today.
I don't have the tools to do more.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.300
And your conclusion?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:51.720
Your Majesty has regular
intercourse with someone.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.470
I trust you can imagine the rest?

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.730
I'm not a woman!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.820
But you are both a woman and a man.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.030
The possibility exists.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.240
With this body?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.160
Such a thing could never be.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.290
Everyone's body is different--unique.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.880
If you need medicine, send for me.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:29.420
Although I'd like you to release me first.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.060
Your Majesty.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.390
Forgive me. I know you depart tomorrow,

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.360
but I wish to return to my estates.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.020
Why?

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.360
I have long been absent.
It seemed a good opportunity.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.450
Farewell.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.920
You are a demon child!
A bloodstained devil!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.340
Richard? Perhaps we should stop.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.470
Anne, ride on ahead of me.
I'll soon catch up.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.050
Very well.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.510
I'll await you in York.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.640
Your Majesty, I will accompany you.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.320
I'll kill whomever you desire.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.910
The answer is obvious.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:41.040
For the throne, and for you.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.580
Buckingham.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.090
I came to speak with you.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.550
Can we be alone somewhere to--

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.760
Inform the chamberlain
that His Majesty has arrived.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.890
Welcome him with all due ceremony.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.020
Where is your wife?

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.770
She is a Woodville.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:08.310
She hasn't shown herself to me
once since your accession.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.570
I'm likely your only ally in this house.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.620
Your house <i>was</i> originally Lancastrian.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.080
But I thought highly of your father.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.870
I need more time.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:30.500
I'm devising the best solution
to our problem.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.800
What was I hoping to hear?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.010
Forgiveness? Apology? Or...

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.180
Very well.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.350
Richard!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.480
No. Words don't matter.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.780
I simply desired to see you.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.030
Are you well?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.660
Henry.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:13.710
I can't remain calm while I'm with you.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.880
I try to set my feelings
aside, but I can't.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:23.600
I cannot bear the mere thought
that anything but me

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.770
has even a tiny place in your heart.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:31.110
Before I know it, I think:

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.190
What can I do...

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.200
What can I do to make you mine alone?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.160
Richard, we can't go on.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.460
You fainted. I shouldn't have pushed you.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:58.050
I'm fine. My physician agrees.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.050
Physician? You summoned Jane?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.300
Yes.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.430
And she found nothing wrong?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.640
Jane said...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:11.310
Your Majesty has regular
intercourse with someone.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.770
I trust you can imagine the rest?

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.900
It's impossible, of course.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.490
If that's true--

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.030
It can't be. It's nightmarish.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:27.040
But if by any chance it is true?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.250
I have that medicine.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.170
--Richard.
--Don't worry.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.130
It's all Jane's absurd fancies.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.760
It's not possible.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.340
More importantly, Henry,

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.970
go to York with me.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.310
I'm to be crowned in my father's city.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.980
I want you at my side.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.400
We won the crown together.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.980
You cut through every briar in my path.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.490
And your health?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.280
I'll be fine, as long as you're with me.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.870
Relaxing has restored my appetite.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.830
I hardly took a bite earlier.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.290
I'll bring food, then.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:18.300
A duke will serve me personally?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.800
He will.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.050
What is this pain?

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.890
I have that medicine.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.930
It feels like something
gouging out my entrails.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:37.480
I tried so many times
to discard my love for you.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:42.530
To cool my head and plot
measures against the prince.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:45.910
All for the crown.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.950
No. No!

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.160
It's all a mistake!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.460
My desire isn't for the crown.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.380
That day we met,

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.670
I wished from the bottom
of my heart for...

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.160
What's going on?!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:30.990
Richard.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.200
Henry, explain yourself.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.000
I'm going to keep you here.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.090
I won't let you go to York.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.510
You won't let me go to York?

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.470
That's right.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.640
What?! Enough nonsense!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.640
It's not nonsense.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.270
With the passage of time, your hair will
grow out like a black veil.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:01.820
Once it covers your shoulders, no one
will recognize you as "King Richard."

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.980
Are you mad?!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.990
I'll let it be known that
the king is gravely ill.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.700
Leave governance to me.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.910
That flimsy excuse won't--

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.870
I know you wanted this too!

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:18.040
That night, our desires
were one and the same.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.090
If you were no longer king,
we could be together always.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:25.510
We needn't give up on loving each other.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.180
Should I go to check on him?

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.180
He promised to return by morning.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.770
His Majesty is a man of his word.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:42.150
I'll take you outside once you calm down.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:45.150
I have beautiful places to show you.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.570
I won't keep you shut up
in a tower forever.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:53.580
I plan to prepare a house where
we can live in secret.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.710
Live with Henry in the woods or somewhere?

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:02.670
Live as an anonymous woman,
unknown to anyone?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:09.680
Taste the golden dew of sleep in
the embrace of gentle warmth?

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.340
That would be far too good for a demon.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:18.310
With love that I thought would
never be within my grasp?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.440
What more could a demon dare to wish for?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.860
What's wrong?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.070
Nothing.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.360
I have something to give you.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.530
Proof that I pledge my soul to you.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.740
What more can I ask for?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.700
Congratulations, Richard.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:40.460
You'll never again shrink, alone and
freezing, from the voices of your curse.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.040
Am I wrong?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:47.880
I did wish to prolong our time
together as long as possible,

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.970
even if it meant discarding
that blood and name.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.100
Even the name of a king.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.730
I already told you. His Majesty
departed this morning.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.190
That can't be true!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:03.100
Ask His Grace again!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.400
Richard.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.990
I was held prisoner many
times in my childhood.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.150
I believe you were as well, Henry.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:17.700
Our lives always belonged
to someone with power.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:22.120
We cursed our impotence
and struggled against fate.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.330
Aren't these the briars
we strove to clear away?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.840
You're right. I did wish.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.090
That's why, that night, I told you plainly

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.180
that I desired the crown
with all my heart.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.640
The future we swore together is...

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.400
Your Majesty!

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.860
Catesby!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.360
I saw you in the window and grew worried.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.820
Duke of Buckingham, explain yourself.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.950
Catesby, sheathe your sword.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:00.830
Unchain me, Buckingham.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.880
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.470
Was it wise to let him go unpunished?

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.720
His crimes are my own.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.850
Follow me when you're ready.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.350
I'll be waiting in York.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.640
He <i>will</i> come to York.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.690
Buckingham is my other half.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.320
Richard,

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.480
what do you truly desire?

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.360
Is that really...

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.070
Is that really your wish?

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:41.540
Once lost, it can never be regained.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:45.290
Will you choose a future of sleepless
nights in the depths of despair

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:50.000
crushed by the weight of what you've lost?

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.420
I'm not the briars that
bind you now, Richard.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:58.180
The blood on your throne
and the "name of a king" are.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.890
Henry,

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.970
have you decided on your wish?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.520
If all goes as planned,

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:11.110
we can meet the royal procession
to York at the church up ahead.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.110
George is buried in that church.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.490
I'll pray for him.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.990
The Lancastrian Edward is there as well.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.120
That's true.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:25.120
Edward. That boy's father.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.420
Does someone you knew rest here?

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.170
My family.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.300
It's so quiet.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:43.640
The clamor of the city and my days
at war seem as though they never were.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.480
Many soldiers perished in this land.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:52.560
Even Prince Edward,
who fought for Lancaster.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.860
I fought here that day myself.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:58.610
It's not much, but accept my contribution.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:03.240
You remind me of Prince Edward's father.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:09.460
King Henry VI was a pious and
compassionate man like you.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.580
Unlike the current king.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:16.050
What sort of man is
the current king, then?

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:20.720
A villain who slew even
his friends and brothers.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:25.810
He would murder even a child
to further his ambitions.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:29.690
Richard III is a demon king.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.900
Yes, he's right.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:36.530
I became a demon,
and all to gain my crown.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:41.070
I ensnared, robbed, and killed
all who stood in my way.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.700
He and I became demons together.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.500
But now...

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.130
Please wait.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.130
Might you be...

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:03.010
The light is overhead.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.510
Your Majesty, King Richard III!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.190
I expect to visit more
frequently from now on.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.190
I'll teach all England who Richard III is.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.690
His name, his face,

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.200
and his power.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.410
The reign of Richard III
is just beginning.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:41.010
Has my sentence been passed,
or have you merely come to torment me,

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.930
Duke of Buckingham?

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:46.010
I'm a sinner, but so are you!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:49.640
You'll get your just deserts in time!

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.020
As you say.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:57.310
I took part in a usurpation
and deceived the innocent.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:02.360
Please forgive me, Your Excellency.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:07.740
Richard is bewitching and charming.
His devilish charisma led me astray.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.120
I took leave of my senses.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.250
I trust you will understand.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.460
O-Of course! You couldn't help it!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:19.210
If Your Grace repents
and turns over a new leaf,

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:22.210
the Lord God will surely forgive you!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:25.430
I came here to do just that.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:30.560
Your Excellency, let us atone
for our sins together.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.850
Henry,

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.560
have you decided on your wish?

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:39.360
Yes. And I'll teach you
what you wish to know.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.160
James Tyrrell,

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.410
kill Richard III.
